{"event": "model_request", "time": 1793347446.2119427, "run_id": "84632ae5b378400c8366c283c8ae348a", "seq": 10, "number": 1, "body": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Complete the task using the Python tools below.\nReturn ONE JSON object with string fields \"thought\" (next action) and \"code\" (executable Python), then STOP.\nExample: {\"thought\":\"Check progress.\",\"code\":\"print(task_status())\"}\nNo Markdown fences, extra JSON, simulated observations or future turns. Keep the action within the output budget.\n\n\nCall tools with keyword arguments. Arrays are Python lists ['a','b'], never encoded strings.\nReads return dicts: r['content'] is text, r['file_hash'] is the edit hash. Commands return r['rc'] and r['stdout'].\nUse print() for needed output. Group independent operations. Variables and imports persist; successful statements\nbefore an error remain executed. Correct the error without restarting completed work.\n\nPaths are relative to the task repository; '.' is its root. Omit cwd for commands there.\nUse tools for all file/command operations. Edit only allowed files, never tests. Use current file_hash as expected_hash.\nFor source edits prefer replace_text_batch with one input hash for unique nonoverlapping edits. Imports allowed: ['collections', 'datetime', 'itertools', 'json', 'math', 'queue', 'random', 're', 'stat', 'statistics', 'time', 'unicodedata']; import before use.\nRead sufficient evidence, preserve relevant findings when useful, implement and verify. Avoid repeated unchanged reads.\nCall final_answer when the requested artifact is ready; missing current-version checks run on that explicit request.\nWhen the current action runs a required test, inspect its actual rc; if it succeeds, update the existing plan\nand call final_answer in the same action when all requirements are satisfied. If it fails, fix the failure instead.\n\nAvailable tools:\n```python\ndef read_file(path: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a text file in full. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids. Read result['content'], not result[:N].\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_pdf(start_page: integer, end_page: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read pages using the repository's read_pdf.py helper. Returns dict: pages (list of {page,text}), evidence_ids, delivery. Extract the required range once; complete pages are sent in bounded batches. Queued ids are not yet read. Do not print all pages.\n\n    Args:\n        start_page: start page\n        end_page: end page\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef run_command(argv: array, cwd: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use '.' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\n\n    Args:\n        argv: argv\n        cwd: cwd\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef update_plan(items: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\n\n    Args:\n        items: List of objects, e.g. [{\"title\":\"Read sources\",\"status\":\"doing\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\n\n    Args:\n        evidence_ids: evidence ids\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef task_status() -> object:\n    \"\"\"Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef save_answer(section: string, question_id: string, answer: object, evidence_id: string, page: integer, quote: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save an answer and exact page quotation. Matching establishes provenance, not semantic support; choose answers and quotes yourself, and ensure every array item is supported.\n\n    Args:\n        section: section\n        question_id: question id\n        answer: Object with exactly one key value, containing a string, integer, or list of strings.\n        evidence_id: evidence id\n        page: page\n        quote: quote\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef save_section(section: string, summary: string, application: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save model-authored section summary and application.\n\n    Args:\n        section: section\n        summary: summary\n        application: application\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef submit_report(overview: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Serialize saved answers and section text into report.json after all five latest notes have been reused.\n\n    Args:\n        overview: overview\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_note(title: string, content: string, evidence_ids: array, section: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence.\n\n    Args:\n        title: Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\n        content: One contiguous string literal, 20..1500 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\n        evidence_ids: Python list[str], e.g. ['ev-abc'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n        section: Required topic: overview/reasoning/tool_use/multi_agent/outlook\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nRead the PDF and update report.json.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"paper\", \"editable\": [\"report.json\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"report.json\"], \"verify_commands\": [], \"required_pages\": [1, 2], \"note_topics\": [\"overview\", \"reasoning\", \"tool_use\", \"multi_agent\", \"outlook\"], \"max_model_calls\": 3}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools.\nWhen the requested work is ready, call final_answer explicitly; it runs missing current-version checks, completes the plan on success, or returns the real failure for repair.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nPaper workflow:\n1. Plan, baseline pytest, read report.json and paper.json; call read_pdf ONCE for the task's full page range.\nThis extracts to local storage and logs read_pdf.py; only bounded batches reach the model. Do not print all pages.\n2. Read the delivered page batches in order. Record a topic's supported findings as soon as useful; do not\nwait until both questions are answered. The next batch follows successful actions automatically. On an\naction error, correct it using the retained batch. Do not call read_pdf/task_status just to advance.\nUse only evidence ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n3. Update the same topic note incrementally, preserving earlier confirmed facts and citations. Each final\ntopic note must contain its two answers, PDF page numbers and continuous exact quotations supporting ALL\nanswer items, within 1500 characters.\nUse write_note(title=..., content=..., evidence_ids=['ev-...'], section='overview') with the actual topic.\n4. Save each question with save_answer(section, question_id, answer={'value': ...}, evidence_id, page, quote).\nChoose answers and citations yourself; exact quotation matching proves provenance only, not that it supports the answer. Every array item must be supported. Save section prose with save_section. After all pages and the latest five notes have appeared together in a later request, call submit_report(overview, expected_hash). Then request final_answer; it runs any missing current-version verification and finishes the plan only on success.\nThis agent already has versioned evidence, bounded page selection, note reuse, tools and verification.\nMulti-agent collaboration and training are future suggestions, not implemented features.\n\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"read\",\"next_requirement\":\"PDF pages not yet sent: 1,2\",\"remaining_count\":7,\"requests_left\":2,\"baseline_done\":0,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":0,\"request_number\":1,\"max_requests\":3,\"requests_after_response\":2,\"first_write_reading_required\":true,\"current_versions\":{\"report.json\":\"44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\"},\"applied_writes\":{},\"verified_versions\":[],\"full_reads_registered\":{\"report.json\":\"44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\"},\"evidence_delivery\":\"Registered full reads are logged tool reads; Evidence headers show selected ranges, whose delivery requires HTTP confirmation.\",\"pdf_pages_missing\":[1,2],\"saved_answers\":{},\"missing_answers\":{\"overview\":[\"categories\",\"search_methods\"],\"reasoning\":[\"self_consistency_selection\",\"tot_search\"],\"tool_use\":[\"toolbench_api_count\",\"toolformer_tools\"],\"multi_agent\":[\"camel_prompting\",\"generative_agents_evaluators\"],\"outlook\":[\"agenda_topics\",\"shared_foundations\"]}}\nEvidence ev-0bb88db782dbb846de19 | report.json | lines:1-1 | sha256=44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\n{}\nEvidence ev-43852c44687baca48e12 | paper.pdf | page:1 | sha256=1b7371417f2dc7bd2b4d16ec6f63bbe53d72dfb4d5c10ef42c2ce9d5394aca5c\nFULL_PAGE_1_\nNot fully delivered yet: ev-4609a2662ec